@startuml task-scheduler
!include state-machine-style.iuml
title Slop Machine | Scheduler admission and per-run volume startup (FR-01 through FR-03, FR-06 / FR-07)
caption A claimed run receives a verified Docker volume/full clone and a credential-ready container before Jira work-start or preflight.

state "Validate scheduler settings\nConfigured limit must be 1, 2 or 3\nResolve Jira backlog/project settings" as Config
state "Task intake\nJira ticket, user prompt or existing task\nSee task-intake.puml" as Intake
state "Wait for new input\nNo task or slot held" as WaitInput
state "Queued\nPersist status; visible to user\nNo execution slot held" as Queue
state Eligibility <<choice>>
state "Wait for capacity\nVisible queued status; no slot" as WaitCapacity
state "Wait for prerequisite\nNo slot; task remains blocked" as WaitDependency <<blocked>>
state "Wait for old run volume recovery\nNo slot; task remains blocked" as WaitWorkspace <<blocked>>
state "Existing active task\nCoalesce duplicate pickup" as Existing
state "Check selected access configuration\nAPI or supported subscription; no token fetched\nSee access-readiness.puml: preclaim_check" as Access
state "Resolve configured target repository\nVerify mapping, remote + target snapshot\nShow project/repository before execution\nSee project-workspace.puml: resolve_for_admission" as Project
state "Atomically claim task + reserve slot\nCheck task/config/target revisions, readiness, active count\nExclude unreconciled old volume; create new run ID" as Claim
state "Create and verify new run volume + full clone\nSystem invokes project-workspace.puml: create_for_run\nTask-owned branch + exclusive volume" as Workspace
state "Start task container\nFetch current selected credential from manager\nVerify agent runtime readiness\nSee access-readiness.puml: worker_start" as WorkerStart
state StartTracking <<choice>>
state "Update Jira: work started\nConfigured active status or progress update\nVerify ticket revision + update" as JiraStart
state "Mark prompt-only task running\nVerify internal status update" as PromptStart
state "Reconcile Jira start update\nRead current ticket; bounded retry" as Reconcile
state "Stop/fence startup container; finalize volume\nReconcile credential, Git + Jira start effects\nInvoke project-workspace.puml: end_run if created\nRelease claim + slot after safe cleanup" as Release
state "Startup cleanup incomplete\nKeep claim/slot; expose recovery action" as CleanupPending <<attention>>
state "Dispatch claimed run to preflight\nAttach secret-free access, repository + volume refs\nTask, source, project + ticket if linked" as Dispatch <<success>>
state "Needs attention\nInvalid config, volume or start update" as Attention <<attention>>
state "Cancelled before dispatch" as Cancelled <<attention>>

[*] --> Config
Config --> Intake : settings valid
Config --> Attention : invalid limit or missing required config
Intake --> Queue : actionable task + tracking record saved
Intake --> WaitInput : no eligible candidate
Intake --> Attention : intake failed
Intake --> Cancelled : prompt cancelled
WaitInput --> Intake : Jira backlog change or new prompt
Queue --> Eligibility : admission check
Queue --> Cancelled : task cancelled
Eligibility --> WaitCapacity : active runs >= configured limit
Eligibility --> WaitDependency : prerequisite unresolved
Eligibility --> WaitWorkspace : old task volume not safely reconciled
Eligibility --> Existing : same task/ticket already active
Eligibility --> Access : eligible and capacity available
WaitCapacity --> Eligibility : slot released or valid limit raised
WaitDependency --> Eligibility : dependency signal received
WaitWorkspace --> Eligibility : old volume reconciled; new run permitted
Access --> Project : selected mode/config supported; evidence recorded
Access --> Attention : setup/auth/limit failure visible; no run started
Project --> Claim : repository identity + target verified;\nproject visible to user
Project --> Attention : mapping, access or target invalid; no run started
Claim --> Workspace : claim + slot + run ID persisted
Claim --> Queue : task revision or claim conflict / refresh
Claim --> Access : access evidence expired or config changed\n/ recheck before claiming
Claim --> Project : repository/target evidence stale\n/ recheck before claiming
Workspace --> WorkerStart : new volume + clone/branch/HEAD verified
Workspace --> Release : creation or verification failed/ambiguous
Workspace --> Release : cancellation requested / reconcile creation effect;\noutcome = cancelled
WorkerStart --> StartTracking : current credential fetched; selected runtime ready
WorkerStart --> Release : credential startup failed or cancelled\n/ reconcile container and volume; outcome recorded
StartTracking --> JiraStart : [Jira ticket linked]
StartTracking --> PromptStart : [prompt-only; no ticket]
StartTracking --> Release : cancellation requested / outcome = cancelled
JiraStart --> Dispatch : Jira start update confirmed
JiraStart --> Reconcile : update failed or result ambiguous
JiraStart --> Release : cancellation requested / reconcile update;\noutcome = cancelled
Reconcile --> JiraStart : retry permitted; effect not applied
Reconcile --> Dispatch : start update already confirmed
Reconcile --> Release : update cannot be confirmed
Reconcile --> Release : cancellation requested / reconcile update;\noutcome = cancelled
PromptStart --> Dispatch : internal running status confirmed
PromptStart --> Release : status update unconfirmed
PromptStart --> Release : cancellation requested / outcome = cancelled
Release --> Attention : [startup failure; cleanup + outcome confirmed]\nclaim/slot released; failure recorded
Release --> Cancelled : [cancel requested; cleanup + outcome confirmed]\nclaim/slot released; cancellation recorded
Release --> CleanupPending : volume/ownership cannot be retired safely
CleanupPending --> Release : bounded recovery restores certainty
Dispatch --> [*] : return dispatched
Existing --> [*] : return existing task; no new run
Attention --> [*] : return attention
Cancelled --> [*] : return cancelled

note right of Claim
  Admission checks and slot reservation are one
  serialized decision. Active runs never exceed 3.
  One task's repair iterations use its existing slot.
  Release happens only after its executor stops/fences.
end note
note right of Workspace
  The coordinator/repository adapter creates the volume and clone.
  Agents receive the verified mount; they do not choose isolation.
  Even a run later closed in preflight has a volume.
  No Jira work-start update occurs until creation and
  container credential startup are confirmed.
  A new run after PR feedback or prerequisite resolution gets
  a new volume/clone after the old run is reconciled.
end note
note bottom of Project
  Pre-claim checks hold no execution slot and fetch no secret.
  Claim revalidates their evidence atomically with capacity and ownership.
  The task container pulls the current selected credential at startup.
  Later auth or repository changes stop affected work for fresh checks.
end note
note bottom of Queue
  Jira and prompt tasks share the same queue and limit.
  Waiting and running statuses are observable.
end note
@enduml
